 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 631809,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stem_html": "<p>Terence looked down the second column of the table below and noticed that <span data-math=\"\\frac{3}{1}=\\frac{9}{3}=\\frac{27}{9}=\\frac{81}{27}\">\\frac{3}{1}=\\frac{9}{3}=\\frac{27}{9}=\\frac{81}{27}</span>. Because of his observation, he claimed that the input-output pairs in this table could be modeled with an exponential function. Explain why Terence is correct or incorrect.&nbsp;</p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr>\n      <th scope=\"col\"><span data-math=\"x\">x</span></th>\n      <th scope=\"col\"><span data-math=\"T(x)\">T(x)</span></th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <td>0</td>\n      <td>1</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>1</td>\n      <td>3</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>4</td>\n      <td>9</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>13</td>\n      <td>27</td>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <td>40</td>\n      <td>81</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1222847,
     "content_html": "Terence is incorrect. This table represents a linear relationship since the ratio of change of each row is consistent."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222844,
     "content_html": "Terence is incorrect. This table represents points that do not have an exponential or linear relationship because the <span data-math=\"x\">x</span> and <span data-math=\"y\">y</span> change by different amounts."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222845,
     "content_html": "Terence is correct. This table can be modeled by <span data-math=\"y=1(3)^x\">y=1(3)^x</span>."
    },
    {
     "id": 1222846,
     "content_html": "Terence is correct. Terms in a table that are connected by a factor are exponential."
    }
   ],
